(83,1,'2025-10-07 19:55:23','2025-10-07 19:55:23','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This is only the beginning! The very first volume of Calvin and Hobbes introduces the world to the most unforgettable duo in comics: Calvin, a wildly imaginative six-year-old, and Hobbes, his sharp-witted tiger companion who springs to life when no one else is watching. Together they mix everyday childhood events with adventure, rebellion, satire, and laughter—whether they’re building mutant snowmen, outsmarting babysitters, or pondering life’s biggest questions under the stars.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Calvin and Hobbes','','publish','closed','closed','','calvin-and-hobbes','','','2025-10-08 00:30:54','2025-10-08 00:30:54','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=83',0,'hh-book','',0),
(84,1,'2025-10-07 19:51:09','2025-10-07 19:51:09','','01_calvin_hobbes','','inherit','open','closed','','01_calvin_hobbes','','','2025-10-07 19:51:09','2025-10-07 19:51:09','',83,'http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/01_calvin_hobbes.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(86,1,'2025-10-07 21:05:56','2025-10-07 21:05:56','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Calvin and Hobbes will always be my besties.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','The best!','','publish','closed','closed','','the-best','','','2025-10-07 21:05:57','2025-10-07 21:05:57','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hhreviews&#038;p=86',0,'hhreviews','',0),
(88,1,'2025-10-08 01:28:01','2025-10-08 01:28:01','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Monsters under the bed, mutant snowmen, and time-travel chaos—Calvin and Hobbes turn ordinary childhood into an extraordinary, heart-filled, philosophical adventure in Something Under the Bed Is Drooling.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In Something Under the Bed Is Drooling, Calvin and Hobbes take childhood imagination to new heights. Hobbes pounces, Susie schemes, and Calvin’s parents endure a nonstop parade of questions, pranks, and musings. Monsters lurk under the bed, snowmen march in grotesque armies, and the cardboard box becomes a springboard for time travel, space adventures, and endless imagination.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Something Under the Bed Is Drooling','','publish','closed','closed','','something-under-the-bed-is-drooling','','','2025-10-08 01:28:02','2025-10-08 01:28:02','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=88',0,'hh-book','',0),
(89,1,'2025-10-08 01:27:55','2025-10-08 01:27:55','','02_something_under_the_bed','','inherit','open','closed','','02_something_under_the_bed','','','2025-10-08 01:27:55','2025-10-08 01:27:55','',88,'http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/02_something_under_the_bed.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(90,1,'2025-10-08 01:41:44','2025-10-08 01:41:44','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Jump into the earliest adventures of an extraordinary duo— mischievous Calvin and his sardonic tiger Hobbes. It’s tuna fish traps, time travel, snowman armies, and schoolyard woes—blending sharp wit, wild imagination, and heartfelt moments in every strip.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Essential Calvin and Hobbes is the perfect introduction to one of the most beloved comic strips of all time. This treasury brings together the first two Calvin and Hobbes collections—Calvin and Hobbes and Something Under the Bed Is Drooling— covering November 18, 1985 to May 23, 1987. The treasury begins with a foreword by Charles M. Schulz, along with a bonus 16-page full-color story exclusive and the illustrated poem, \"A Nauseous Nocturne.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','The Essential Calvin and Hobbes: A Calvin and Hobbes Treasury','','publish','closed','closed','','the-essential-calvin-and-hobbes-a-calvin-and-hobbes-treasury','','','2025-10-08 01:41:45','2025-10-08 01:41:45','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=90',0,'hh-book','',0),
(91,1,'2025-10-08 01:41:38','2025-10-08 01:41:38','','03_essential','','inherit','open','closed','','03_essential','','','2025-10-08 01:41:38','2025-10-08 01:41:38','',90,'http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/03_essential.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(92,1,'2025-10-08 02:06:47','2025-10-08 02:06:47','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Of course homework can wait—the Yukon is calling! Join Calvin and Hobbes for cosmic battles, camping blunders, razor-sharp laughs, and more wild adventures depicting the unforgettable charm of childhood rebellion in Yukon Ho!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>There’s only one reasonable response to chores, baths, and homework: escape to the Yukon with your tiger best friend.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In Yukon Ho!, the series’ core characters are now familiar faces: Spaceman Spiff, Miss Wormwood, neighbor Susie, Rosalyn the babysitter, and Calvin’s endlessly patient, frequently exasperated parents. Here, Bill Watterson also sharpens the strip’s signature themes—nature vs. technology, imagination vs. reality, childhood vs. adulthood—while delivering backyard battles, camping mishaps, and late-night philosophizing on everything from pollution to human folly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Yukon Ho!','','publish','closed','closed','','yukon-ho','','','2025-10-08 02:06:47','2025-10-08 02:06:47','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=92',0,'hh-book','',0),
(93,1,'2025-10-08 02:06:40','2025-10-08 02:06:40','','04_yukon_ho','','inherit','open','closed','','04_yukon_ho','','','2025-10-08 02:06:40','2025-10-08 02:06:40','',92,'http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/04_yukon_ho.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(94,1,'2025-10-08 02:23:37','2025-10-08 02:23:37','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A colorful celebration of Calvin’s wildest adventures, The Calvin and Hobbes Lazy Sunday Book features full-color Sunday strips packed with humor, heart, and tiger-powered mischief—perfect for comic lovers, collectors, and daydreamers of all ages.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Calvin and Hobbes Lazy Sunday Book collects every Sunday strip from May 24, 1987, to July 30, 1989, showcasing Calvin’s adventures in vibrant full color. From imaginative space missions to snowman armies and philosophical debates, Watterson’s expansive Sunday panels artistically showcase the creativity and charm of a boy and his tiger.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A favorite of readers young and old, this collection also features fan-favorite storylines and a ten-page Spaceman Spiff adventure, a redrawn classic strip, and an afterword from Bill Watterson. Whether revisiting childhood favorites or discovering Calvin and Hobbes for the first time, readers will delight in this nostalgic tribute to imagination, friendship, and mischief.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','The Calvin and Hobbes Lazy Sunday Book','','publish','closed','closed','','the-calvin-and-hobbes-lazy-sunday-book','','','2025-10-08 02:23:37','2025-10-08 02:23:37','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=94',0,'hh-book','',0),
(95,1,'2025-10-08 02:23:30','2025-10-08 02:23:30','','05_a_collection_of_sunday','','inherit','open','closed','','05_a_collection_of_sunday','','','2025-10-08 02:23:30','2025-10-08 02:23:30','',94,'http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/05_a_collection_of_sunday.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(96,1,'2025-10-08 02:37:22','2025-10-08 02:37:22','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>From interplanetary escapes to snowman invasions, Weirdos from Another Planet! is packed with laugh-out-loud comics and signature Calvin and Hobbes chaos—perfect for fans of wild imagination and childhood fun.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Calvin and Hobbes take imagination to bold new heights in Weirdos from Another Planet!, with comics spanning February to December 1988. Calvin launches the G.R.O.S.S. Club to torment Susie, pilots imaginary spaceships on cosmic adventures, and channels alter-egos like Tracer Bullet to battle the everyday boredom of childhood. Mischief, wit, and invention fuel every page.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Weirdos from Another Planet!','','publish','closed','closed','','weirdos-from-another-planet','','','2025-10-08 02:37:22','2025-10-08 02:37:22','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=96',0,'hh-book','',0),
(97,1,'2025-10-08 02:32:07','2025-10-08 02:32:07','','Version 1.0.0','Version 1.0.0','inherit','open','closed','','version-1-0-0','','','2025-10-08 02:32:07','2025-10-08 02:32:07','',96,'http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/06_weirdos_from_another_planet.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),
(98,1,'2025-10-08 03:50:53','2025-10-08 03:50:53','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This large-format treasury collects every strip from Yukon Ho! and Weirdos from Another Planet!, with full-color Sundays and the debut of Calvin’s infamous duplicator—a must-have for readers who love mischief, imagination, and tiger-powered mayhem.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>What happens when bath time becomes a Yukon expedition—or school avoidance turns into interplanetary travel?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Authoritative Calvin and Hobbes is a must-have treasury for fans of Bill Watterson’s legendary comic strip. This large-format volume collects every strip from Yukon Ho! and Weirdos from Another Planet! (spanning May 24, 1987 to December 4, 1988), including both black-and-white dailies and full-color Sundays. It also features a full-color story unique to this collection.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','The Authoritative Calvin and Hobbes','','publish','closed','closed','','the-authoritative-calvin-and-hobbes','','','2025-10-08 03:50:53','2025-10-08 03:50:53','',0,'http://localhost/?post_type=hh-book&#038;p=98',0,'hh-book','',0),
